  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is given that&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>The relation between the electric, magnetic field and speed of light is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0031_397a2f149a54.png\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 246px;\" /><br />Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Using the relation,<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>"
  }
